@startuml automation-use-cases
!include _theme.iuml
left to right direction

actor "Automation workflow" as Automation
actor "Integrating application" as Application

rectangle "Octoform 0.4 · non-interactive use" {
  package "Reachable without a prompt" {
    usecase "validateConfiguration()" as Validate
    usecase "auditRepositories()" as Audit
    usecase "planChanges()" as Plan
    usecase "savePlan()" as Save
  }
  package "Reachable only with --yes" {
    usecase "applyPlan()" as Apply
    usecase "applySavedPlan()" as ApplySaved
  }
  usecase "embedGovernanceServices()" as Embed
}

Automation --> Validate
Automation --> Audit
Automation --> Plan
Automation --> Save
Automation --> Apply
Automation --> ApplySaved
Application --> Embed

Apply ..> Plan : <<include>>
ApplySaved ..> Save : <<include>>

note bottom of Embed
  An automation workflow is the same actor role as an operator
  minus the ability to answer a prompt. It reaches the same use
  cases; --yes replaces the confirmation step, so the review it
  represents has to exist outside Octoform.

  An integrating application calls exported functions directly
  and therefore owns authentication, invocation and error
  handling around them.
end note
@enduml
